Before spawning a new child conversation, **check `{{ .Children.MCPText }}`**
(the existing children list) and **skip spawning** if a child already exists
for the same PR + task (e.g. a child titled `Fix CI for PR #<number>` is
still running, or was updated after the failing CI run that would trigger a
new spawn). The previous run already created it and it may still be
working.

**Spawn cap:** spawn at most **3 conversations per run**. Spawned
conversations are one-off and **must never be loops** — do not call
`mitto_conversation_set_loop` on them and never pass `loop_prompt` /
`loop_frequency_*` when creating them.
